From 9fa1978f656e78e2c94d6fe626b67fc94033ee3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:38:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/29] CI: run the probe ABI check and the adapter suite, so
 'green' means they ran

Claimed wired in the commit before last; it was not. The patch asserting on an indentation
difference had failed and I moved on without re-reading the workflow, and a passing build proved
nothing about steps that were never in it. So this says how it is verified: after pushing, grep
the workflow for run_adapter_tests, and after the run, grep its log for the suites' own output -
not just the conclusion.

The guard workflow now clones Vulkan-Headers into RUNNER_TEMP and exports VULKAN_INCLUDE_DIR for
both suites: run_probe_tests.sh gains the real-ABI struct check (58 declarations) that its mock
cannot provide, and run_adapter_tests.sh runs the fake backend that SIGKILLs itself inside
vkQueuePresentKHR. Both need seconds and neither needs a GPU.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml b/.github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml
index 2389f3f..a20dae0 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/gpu-guard-ci.yml
@@ -49,8 +49,16 @@ jobs:
             test -f tools/linuxfs/overlay/usr/local/bin/droiddeck-gpu-probe
             # Before the app: the probe decides whether Steam may touch the GPU at all, and it has
             # twice shipped broken in ways that only showed up on the phone. It is tested here
-            # against a fake loader, which needs no GPU and takes seconds.
+            # against a fake loader, which needs no GPU and takes seconds. The headers are cloned
+            # because the probe's hand-written structs are then checked against the real Vulkan ABI
+            # (tools/test/vulkan_offsets.c) instead of against the mock that has been agreeing with
+            # them - a layout wrong by 16 bytes looks perfectly sane and is only fatal on the phone.
+            git clone -q --depth 1 https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Headers "$RUNNER_TEMP/vkh"
+            export VULKAN_INCLUDE_DIR="$RUNNER_TEMP/vkh/include"
             bash tools/test/run_probe_tests.sh
+            # And the adapter's own suite: a fake backend that can SIGKILL itself mid-present is the
+            # only way to prove the trace survives a dying process with the dying call last.
+            bash drivers/mali-g615/test/run_adapter_tests.sh
             bash tools/build_local.sh
           } 2>&1 | tee /tmp/droiddeck-build.log
       # The machine working on this branch cannot download Actions logs, only talk to the API, so
